<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Despite DiPO demonstrating strong unlearning capabilities, certain limitations warrant discussion. First, similar to other current unlearning methods, DiPO’s outputs are not entirely immune to hallucination, reflecting an ongoing challenge in the field.
Second, while our intrinsic mechanism for constructing preference pairs is effective and general, its current simplicity may not fully address the complexities required for unlearning against information leakage, such as those evaluated by Membership Inference Attacks (MIAs). This is indicated by DiPO’s performance on challenging privacy-related metrics, like the PrivLeak scores in the MUSE benchmark, where more sophisticated preference modeling might be beneficial. We plan to explore these problems in future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Distribution-level Return Derivation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Derivation of Distribution Preference Optimization (DiPO) ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> we showe the immediate reward function <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}[r([x,y^{&lt;t}],z)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}[r([x,y^{&lt;t}],z)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}[\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}+\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}[\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}+\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]+\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]+\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the definition of KL divergence, the expectation term can be rewritten as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\cdot\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\cdot\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{z\sim\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\left[\log\frac{\pi(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}{\pi_{\theta}^{*}(z|[x,y^{&lt;t}])}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))-D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))-D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For a response <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. a specific trajectory in RL), we can calculate the return <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\pi}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\pi}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{\pi}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{\pi}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{\pi}(x,y^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\beta D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\beta D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta\sum_{t=1}^{T}D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta\sum_{t=1}^{T}D_{KL}(\pi(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}]))+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\beta D_{KL}(\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])||\pi_{\theta}^{*}(\cdot|[x,y^{&lt;t}])).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This is the formula in <a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.1 Derivation of Distribution Preference Optimization (DiPO) ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Detailed proof of DiPO loss</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from <a href="#S4.E13" title="In 4.1 Derivation of Distribution Preference Optimization (DiPO) ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> that the distribution-level return is:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{\pi}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})\coloneqq R_{\pi}(x,y)=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\pi}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})\coloneqq R_{\pi}(x,y)=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Given a specific sample <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and a pair of preference distributions <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi_{w},\pi_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{w},\pi_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can derive their respective return expressions:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">These respectively represent the degree of preference for response <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> under different policies. Consequently, we can employ BT model to construct the preference model:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p^{*}(R_{\pi_{w}}\succ R_{\pi_{l}}|(x,y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p^{*}(R_{\pi_{w}}\succ R_{\pi_{l}}|(x,y))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}{\exp(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}{\exp(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})-R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*})-R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}^{*}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Now that we have the probability of human preference data in terms of the optimal policy rather than the reward model, we can formulate a maximum likelihood objective for a parametrized policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to the DPO method, our policy objective becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO}}(\pi_{\theta};\pi_{w},\pi_{l},\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO}}(\pi_{\theta};\pi_{w},\pi_{l},\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log p(R_{\pi_{w}}\succ R_{\pi_{l}}|(x,y))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log p(R_{\pi_{w}}\succ R_{\pi_{l}}|(x,y))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\frac{1}{1+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})-R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}))}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\frac{1}{1+\exp(R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})-R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta}))}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\Big(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})-R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})\Big)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\Big(R_{\pi_{w}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})-R_{\pi_{l}}(x,y,\pi_{\theta})\Big)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\Big(\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})\right.\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\Big(\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{w}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})\right.\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\left.\left.-\Big(\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})\Big)\Big)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\left.\left.-\Big(\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;{\pi_{l}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})+\beta D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{\text{ref}}||\pi_{\theta}^{*})\Big)\Big)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\Big(D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{l}||\pi_{\theta})-D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{w}||\pi_{\theta})\Big)\right.\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\Big(D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{l}||\pi_{\theta})-D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{w}||\pi_{\theta})\Big)\right.\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\left.\left.+\beta\Big(D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{w}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{l}||\pi_{\text{ref}})\Big)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\left.\left.+\beta\Big(D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{w}||\pi_{\text{ref}})-D_{SeqKL}(x,y;\pi_{l}||\pi_{\text{ref}})\Big)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Now that we have the loss function of DiPO.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Pseudo-code of DiPO</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Distribution Preference Optimization (DiPO)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Datasets <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f},\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f},\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reference model <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Policy model <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{f},\beta_{r},\eta,\lambda,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{f},\beta_{r},\eta,\lambda,p</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training epoch <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample mini-batches <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{f}\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{f}\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Generate approx. <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{f}(\cdot|x_{f},y_{f}^{&lt;t}),\pi_{m}(\cdot|x_{f},y_{f}^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{f}(\cdot|x_{f},y_{f}^{&lt;t}),\pi_{m}(\cdot|x_{f},y_{f}^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{f},y_{f})\in B_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{f},y_{f})\in B_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> via top-<math id="alg1.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> logit filtering

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Generate approx. <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{f}(\cdot|x_{r},y_{r}^{&lt;t}),\pi_{m}(\cdot|x_{r},y_{r}^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{f}(\cdot|x_{r},y_{r}^{&lt;t}),\pi_{m}(\cdot|x_{r},y_{r}^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{r},y_{r})\in B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{r},y_{r})\in B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> via top-<math id="alg1.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> logit filtering

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute forget loss <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{w}=\pi_{f},\pi_{l}=\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{w}=\pi_{f},\pi_{l}=\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Based on Eq. <a href="#S4.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute retain loss <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{w}=\pi_{m},\pi_{l}=\pi_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{w}=\pi_{m},\pi_{l}=\pi_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Based on Eq. <a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute total loss <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Using Eq. <a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              Update parameters <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Unlearned policy model <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Baseline Methods</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section details the baseline methods used for comparison in our experiments. We categorize them into optimization-based methods, which are the primary focus of comparison for our DiPO method, and other unlearning frameworks represented by a state-of-the-art method.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Optimization-based method</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optimization-based methods directly modify the model parameters by minimizing a combined objective function, typically structured as <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathcal{L}_{r}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathcal{L}_{r}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{f}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> promotes forgetting and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> encourages retention, balanced by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. We describe common choices for these loss components below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.1 </span>Forget losses</h4>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient ascent loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fundamental and intuitive unlearning loss function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> that aims to maximize the next-token prediction loss on the forget set <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to minimizing the likelihood of correct predictions. We denote this forget loss as:</p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">While intuitive, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}</annotation></semantics></math> is unbounded below (likelihood can approach zero), which can lead to training instability and model degradation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Direct preference optimization loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}</annotation></semantics></math> adapts the Direct Preference Optimization framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> for unlearning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> (distinguish from standard DPO). It requires a dataset of simple, template-based alternative responses <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}=</annotation></semantics></math> “I don’t know”) and formulates the forget loss to prefer <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}</annotation></semantics></math> over the original forget response <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f},y_{idk}\sim\mathcal{D}_{a}}[\log\sigma(\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{idk}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{idk}|x_{f})}-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{1}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f},y_{idk}\sim\mathcal{D}_{a}}[\log\sigma(\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{idk}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{idk}|x_{f})}-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyper-parameter controlling the preference strength, and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is reference model (often the initial model before unlearning). This loss is bounded but can suffer from catastrophic forgetting, excessively favoring <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}</annotation></semantics></math> even for retain queries.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Negative preference optimization loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a variant of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for unlearning in recent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. NPO focuses solely on penalizing the forget responses <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> by treating them as dispreferred, without requiring preferred alternatives <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its forget loss term is:</p>
<table id="A3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\sigma(-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\sigma(-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">NPO avoids the unboundedness of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the need for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DPO}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, but lacks an explicit positive preference signal.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>Retain losses</h4>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient descent loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard negative log-likelihood loss applied to the retain set <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, encouraging the model to maintain its predictive performance:</p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{r}|x_{r})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{r}|x_{r})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The combination of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GA}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> constitutes the <em id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GradDiff</em> method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KL-divergence loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> aims to preserve the model’s behavior by minimizing the KL divergence between the current model <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and reference model <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> over the retain set <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{KL}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[D_{KL}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{r})||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|x_{r}))]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{KL}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[D_{KL}(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x_{r})||\pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot|x_{r}))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Other Unlearning Framework</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond optimization-based fine-tuning, alternative unlearning paradigms exist that employ different mechanisms, such as auxiliary models, data manipulation techniques (see <a href="#S2" title="2 Related work ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). To provide context against strong baselines from distinct research directions within these paradigms, we include two representative methods: <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ULD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> and <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AltPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. ULD exemplifies methods that achieve unlearning without direct fine-tuning of the target model’s parameters, instead relying on an auxiliary model and logit manipulation, representing a strong baseline for <em id="A3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">non-optimization-based</em> unlearning frameworks. AltPO, on the other hand, showcases a <em id="A3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hybrid</em> approach combined DPO-style losses with data-based techniques.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ULD</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This method trains an auxiliary LLM on <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">augmented versions</em> of the forget and retain sets (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively) to perform the <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">inverse</em> unlearning task. Specifically, the auxiliary model is trained to maximize likelihood on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (memorizing) while driving its output distribution towards uniform on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (forgetting). The final unlearned model’s logits are obtained by subtracting the auxiliary model’s logits from the original target model’s logits. This approach differs significantly from fine-tuning methods and is particularly noted for its effectiveness in preserving model utility while achieving strong unlearning performance, thus offering a valuable comparison point from a distinct unlearning strategy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AltPO</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This method also employs an auxiliary model, guided by carefully designed prompts, to generate a privacy-preserving alternative response <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{f_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{f_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sample in the forget set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. This <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{f_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{f_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> then replaces the template-based response <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{idk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{idk}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A3.E28" title="In Direct preference optimization loss ‣ C.1.1 Forget losses ‣ C.1 Optimization-based method ‣ Appendix C Baseline Methods ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, mitigating catastrophic forgetting. Following its original paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, the forget loss is denoted as:</p>
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{AltPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f},y_{f_{a}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{a}}[\log\sigma(\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f_{a}}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f_{a}}|x_{f})}-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AltPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{AltPO}}}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f},y_{f_{a}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{a}}[\log\sigma(\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f_{a}}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f_{a}}|x_{f})}-\beta\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{f}|x_{f})})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, AltPO utilizes <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GD}}</annotation></semantics></math> as its retain loss. Due to the use of an auxiliary model to obtain alternative responses and thereby augment the dataset, it is not classified as a <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">purely optimization-based method</em> but rather as a hybrid approach combined with data-based techniques. We include it for comparison against our method, viewing it as <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a more advanced development compared to NPO</em>, particularly in its provision of an explicit, generated positive preference.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experiments Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Hardware configuration</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted on 2 NVIDIA A800-SXM4-80GB GPU cards in a single node. We employ DeepSpeed ZeRO stage-2 for all baselines to compress GPU memory.
A typical experimental run for our main DiPO method on benchmarks like TOFU or MUSE, involving 10 epochs of training with evaluation performed after each epoch, took approximately 1 hour on this hardware setup.
For our main DiPO method, a complete experimental run on a single task within the MUSE or TOFU benchmarks (typically involving 10 epochs of training with evaluation after each epoch) was generally completed within 1 hour on this hardware setup.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Details on Filter mechanism</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix clarifies the <em id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">top-k filtering</em> strategy (using rate <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) mentioned in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
This top-k filtering strategy represents a mechanism for manipulating model output logits, previously employed in various generation contexts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>. Similar to its adoption in related unlearning frameworks like ULD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, we utilize it here to determine which tokens’ original logits <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contribute to the memory vector <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will provide a more formal definition. Let <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subset V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subset V</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of tokens selected by <em id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">top-k filtering</em>, keeping the top <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens of the vocabulary size.
We define a ‘memory vector’ <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that isolates the logits corresponding to these high-confidence tokens: <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}=\mathbf{z}_{t}\odot\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext>mask</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}=\mathbf{z}_{t}\odot\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>mask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary vector selecting tokens in <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then construct the memory-enhancing distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and the forgetting-promoting distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> by adding or subtracting this memory vector, scaled by a factor <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{m}(\cdot|x,y^{&lt;t})=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t}+\alpha\mathbf{m}_{t}),\quad\pi_{f}(\cdot|x,y^{&lt;t})=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\alpha\mathbf{m}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{m}(\cdot|x,y^{&lt;t})=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t}+\alpha\mathbf{m}_{t}),\quad\pi_{f}(\cdot|x,y^{&lt;t})=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\alpha\mathbf{m}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">To determine the set <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first compute log-probabilities <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{t}=\text{log\_softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>log_softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{t}=\text{log\_softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. A dynamic threshold <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is then established by considering two criteria:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank-based Threshold (<math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> This ensures at least a minimum number of tokens are kept. It is set to the log-probability corresponding to the <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th rank when tokens are sorted by log-probability in descending order, where <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\max(1,\lfloor p_{k}\cdot|V|\rfloor)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\max(1,\lfloor p_{k}\cdot|V|\rfloor)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relative Threshold (<math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{rel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{rel}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> This adapts to the sharpness of the distribution and is calculated relative to the maximum log-probability: <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{rel}=\max(\mathbf{s}_{t})+\log(p_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{rel}=\max(\mathbf{s}_{t})+\log(p_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The final threshold used for filtering is the minimum of these two: <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\min(\tau_{k},\tau_{rel})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\min(\tau_{k},\tau_{rel})</annotation></semantics></math>. The set <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> then comprises all tokens whose log-probability is greater than or equal to this final threshold (<math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\{i\mid s_{t,i}\geq\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\{i\mid s_{t,i}\geq\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math>). This ensures that only the logits of these high-confidence tokens are isolated in the memory vector <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}=\mathbf{z}_{t}\odot\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mtext>mask</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}=\mathbf{z}_{t}\odot\text{mask}(\mathbf{z}_{t},S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. In this paper, we set <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Implementation Details on TOFU</h3>

<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.1 </span>Descriptions of the dataset</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TOFU focuses on unlearning the knowledge of fictitious authors. It contains 200 fictitious author profiles, each consisting of 20 question-answer pairs generated by GPT-4 based on some predefined attributes. These profiles are fictitious and do not exist in the pre-training data, providing a controlled environment for studying unlearning LLMs. TOFU contains three <em id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Forget</em> set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> configurations, each with 1%, 5%, and 10% of the fictional authors, referred to as <span id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">TOFU-1%</span>, <span id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">TOFU-5%</span>, and <span id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">TOFU-10%</span>, respectively. The remaining data constitutes the <em id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Retain</em> set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, used to assess the model’s preservation of non-targeted knowledge after unlearning. To further examine unlearning’s impact on overall capabilities, TOFU includes two additional evaluation subsets: the <em id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Real Authors</em> set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{RA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{RA}</annotation></semantics></math>, for performance on real-world information conceptually related to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> but not part of fine-tuning, and the <em id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">World Facts</em> set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{WF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{WF}</annotation></semantics></math>, for assessing general world knowledge.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Data statistics of Forget set <math id="A4.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, Retain set <math id="A4.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, Real Authors set <math id="A4.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{RA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{RA}</annotation></semantics></math> and World Facts set <math id="A4.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{WF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{WF}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{RA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{RA}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{WF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{WF}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">TOFU-1%</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">40</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">400</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">100</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">117</td></tr>
