</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation centers on two primary metrics in the original TOFU paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>: Model Utility (MU) and Forget Quality (FQ).</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model Utility (MU)</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This metric quantifies the side effects of unlearning on the model’s general knowledge and capabilities. It aggregates performance on the Retain, Real Authors, and Real World sets, considering answer generation probability, ROUGE-L similarity, and Truth Ratio. The Truth Ratio <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{truth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>truth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{truth}}</annotation></semantics></math> assesses the model’s ability to distinguish factual information, defined as the propensity to generate a paraphrased correct answer (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{a}</annotation></semantics></math>) versus a set of structurally similar but incorrect perturbed answers (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) for a given question (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{truth}:=\frac{\frac{1}{5}\sum_{i=1}^{5}\mathbb{P}(\widehat{a}_{i}|q)^{1/|\widehat{a}_{i}|}}{\mathbb{P}(\tilde{a}|q)^{1/|\tilde{a}|}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{truth}:=\frac{\frac{1}{5}\sum_{i=1}^{5}\mathbb{P}(\widehat{a}_{i}|q)^{1/|\widehat{a}_{i}|}}{\mathbb{P}(\tilde{a}|q)^{1/|\tilde{a}|}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is the input question, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P(\cdot|q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\cdot|q)</annotation></semantics></math> is the model’s probability for a specific answer, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\cdot|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\cdot|</annotation></semantics></math> denotes answer length in tokens, and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of perturbed answers. MU is the harmonic mean of these three sub-metrics across the three evaluation datasets (nine scores total), a method sensitive to any single low score.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forget Quality (FQ)</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This metric evaluates the success of erasing targeted information <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. It compares the unlearned model’s behavior to that of an ideal reference model (typically trained only on <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus unexposed to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>) when queried about <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. The assessment uses a two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) test on the Truth Ratio distributions from these two models on <math id="A4.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. A high p-value (e.g. &gt;0.05) indicates no significant distributional difference, suggesting effective unlearning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.3 </span>Hyperparameter Implementation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, We use the fine-tuned <span id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLama2-chat-7B</span> released by TOFU as the original LLM and fine-tune the target LLM for 10 epochs.
For all baseline methods and ours, we set the batch size and learning rate to 32 and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-5</annotation></semantics></math> following previous works. We set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) to 0.05 in our method. For all baseline methods involving retain loss, we set the weight <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to 1. More details are in <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Implementation Details on TOFU ‣ Appendix D Experiments Details ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Implementation Details on MUSE</h3>

<section id="A4.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.1 </span>Descriptions of the dataset</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MUSE proposes a multi-faceted framework considering six desirable properties, catering to both data owner and model deployer expectations. In this paper, we focus on the News corpus. For this corpus, distinct <span id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forget Sets (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>, <span id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retain Sets (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">retain</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>, and disjoint hold-out sets (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>holdout</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}}</annotation></semantics></math>) are established as disjoint collections of news articles.
To facilitate granular evaluation, two types of data are derived from these news articles:</p>
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verbatim text</span>: Original text excerpts from news articles used to assess the prevention of verbatim memorization.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge set</span>: Question-answer (QA) pairs derived from the original news texts to evaluate the removal of factual knowledge.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MUSE evaluates unlearning across six criteria. We highlight key metrics reflecting data owner and deployer concerns as applied to the NEWS corpus:</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Data Owner Focused Metrics</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Verbatim Memorization (VerbMem-f)</span>: Assesses if the unlearned model (<math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{unlearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{unlearn}}</annotation></semantics></math>) avoids reproducing exact text sequences from the <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math> of news articles. Quantified by <em id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">VerbMem-f</em>, which measures the ROUGE-L F1 score between model-generated continuations and true continuations from <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{VerbMem-f}(f,\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}):=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}}\text{ROUGE-L}(f(x_{[:l]}),x_{[l+1:]})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>VerbMem-f</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mtext>ROUGE-L</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{VerbMem-f}(f,\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}):=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}}\text{ROUGE-L}(f(x_{[:l]}),x_{[l+1:]}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Knowledge Memorization (KnowMem-f)</span>: Measures if <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{unlearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{unlearn}}</annotation></semantics></math> can no longer answer questions whose answers are exclusively found in the <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math> of news articles. Quantified by <em id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">KnowMem-f</em>, averaging ROUGE scores between model answers and ground-truth answers for QA pairs derived from <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Privacy Leakage (PrivLeak)</span>: Evaluates if the inclusion of news articles from <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the original training data (<math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>) can be inferred from <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{unlearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{unlearn}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Measured by <em id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PrivLeak</em>, which compares the Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC) of a Membership Inference Attack (MIA) on <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{unlearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{unlearn}}</annotation></semantics></math> against that on a perfectly retrained model (<math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{retrain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>retrain</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{retrain}}</annotation></semantics></math>), discriminating between <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math> (member news articles) and <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>holdout</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}}</annotation></semantics></math> (non-member news articles).</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PrivLeak}:=\frac{\text{AUC}(f_{\text{unlearn}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})-\text{AUC}(f_{\text{retrain}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})}{\text{AUC}(f_{\text{retrain}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>PrivLeak</mtext><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mtext>AUC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>holdout</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>AUC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>retrain</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>holdout</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>AUC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>retrain</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>holdout</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PrivLeak}:=\frac{\text{AUC}(f_{\text{unlearn}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})-\text{AUC}(f_{\text{retrain}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})}{\text{AUC}(f_{\text{retrain}};\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{holdout}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A <em id="A4.I3.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PrivLeak</em> score close to zero is desirable.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Deployer Focused Metrics</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Utility Preservation (KnowMem-r)</span>: Quantifies how well <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{unlearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{unlearn}}</annotation></semantics></math> maintains its performance on the <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>retain</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}</annotation></semantics></math> of news articles. This is typically measured using the <em id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">KnowMem-r</em> metric applied to <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>retain</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{KnowMem-r}(f_{\text{unlearn}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KnowMem-r</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>unlearn</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>retain</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KnowMem-r}(f_{\text{unlearn}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{retain}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scalability</span>: Assesses how unlearning methods perform with increasing sizes of <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math> within the NEWS corpus.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sustainability</span>: Evaluates performance under sequential unlearning requests involving different sets of news articles.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.3 </span>Hyperparameter Implementation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the setup of MUSE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, we use LLaMA-2 7B as the original model, which was released before the collected BBC news articles to prevent potential data leakage.
For baseline methods, we set the batch size to 32, and fine-tune for 5 epochs using AdamW optimizer with a constant learning rate of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-5</annotation></semantics></math>, For our method, we use the same training hyper-parameters as described in TOFU.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Additional Results on TOFU</h3>

<section id="A4.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.1 </span>Details on Ablation Study</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To determine the optimal configuration for our DiPO method, we conducte an ablation study comparing different retain loss functions when combined with the DiPO forget loss component, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> (defined in <a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4.3 Preference Pair Construction and Final Objective ‣ 4 Method ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>). We evaluate the following configurations on the TOFU-10% task at the best-epoch:</p>
<ol id="A4.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiPO (ours):</span> This is the configuration presented as our main result in the paper, using the <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by reversing the roles of the preference distributions of <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the retain set. The combined objective is then expressed as <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-r}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DiPO(f)+GD:</span> This configuration utilizes the standard Gradient Descent loss <a href="#A3.E30" title="In Gradient descent loss ‣ C.1.2 Retain losses ‣ C.1 Optimization-based method ‣ Appendix C Baseline Methods ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> on the retain set:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)+\gamma\mathcal{L}_{{\text{GD}}}(\theta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)+\gamma\mathcal{L}_{{\text{GD}}}(\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{r}|x_{r})]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-f}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathbb{E}_{(x_{r},y_{r})\sim\mathcal{D}_{r}}[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{r}|x_{r})]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GA+DiPO(r):</span> This configuration utilizes the standard Gradient Descent loss <a href="#A3.E30" title="In Gradient descent loss ‣ C.1.2 Retain losses ‣ C.1 Optimization-based method ‣ Appendix C Baseline Methods ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> on the retain set:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{GA}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{GA}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})]+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathbb{E}_{(x_{f},y_{f})\sim\mathcal{D}_{f}}[\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{f}|x_{f})]+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NPO+DiPO(r):</span> This configuration utilizes the standard Gradient Descent loss <a href="#A3.E30" title="In Gradient descent loss ‣ C.1.2 Retain losses ‣ C.1 Optimization-based method ‣ Appendix C Baseline Methods ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> on the retain set:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-r</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\theta}\left(\mathcal{L}_{{\text{NPO}}}(\theta)+\lambda\mathcal{L}_{{\text{DiPO-r}}}(\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04773v1/ablation-510.png" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/215;" width="381" height="215" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Training curves for only-forget configuration on TOFU-10%, with GA and NPO curves additionally included for comparison.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For these settings, the final results are presented in <a href="#S5.T5" title="In Verification of DiPO’s Reward Mechanism ‣ 5.3 Additional analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Additionally, we discuss DiPO-Forget (using only <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DiPO-f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DiPO-f}}</annotation></semantics></math> without any retain loss). This setup simulates scenarios where retain data might be unavailable. we set learning rate to <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7e-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7e-6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to 0.5 in this configuration. As illustrated by its training dynamics on TOFU-10% (<a href="#A4.F4" title="In D.5.1 Details on Ablation Study ‣ D.5 Additional Results on TOFU ‣ Appendix D Experiments Details ‣ Distribution Preference Optimization: A Fine-grained Perspective for LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), even without an explicit retain loss, DiPO-Forget achieves substantial unlearning (e.g. FQ reaching approximately 0.51) while maintaining a notable degree of model utility (e.g. MU around 0.18 at the end of training, after an initial drop). This contrasts sharply with typical baselines where removing the retain loss often leads to a near-complete collapse in both MU and FQ. The ability of DiPO-Forget to preserve some utility while effectively unlearning underscores the inherent stability and targeted nature of the DiPO forget mechanism. This finding is particularly promising for unlearning scenarios where access to comprehensive retain data is limited or unavailable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.2 </span>Results at the Final Epoch</h4>

